  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44245110",
      "title": "Module Introduction",
      "sourceHash": "972339752e72f88fd1e002911e051775ef2198555707c506c0462cf09a855f71",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.89,
          "en": "In the previous course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.89,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "you learned in detail how you can handle form submissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 13.32,
          "en": "and user input in React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 17.244,
          "en": "In this section, we're kind of building up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.244,
          "end": 19.44,
          "en": "on what you learned there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 24.21,
          "en": "and we'll explore a different way of handling user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.21,
          "end": 28.38,
          "en": "Because in this section, we'll explore form actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.38,
          "end": 32.79,
          "en": "a feature that's actually built into React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.79,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "at least if you're using React 19 or higher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "So it's a relatively new feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 43.68,
          "en": "It's not part of older React versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.68,
          "end": 46.68,
          "en": "but if you are working in a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.68,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "that uses at least version 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 53.19,
          "en": "you can use this form actions feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.19,
          "end": 56.07,
          "en": "about which you will learn in this section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "instead of handling form submissions manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "as you learned it in the previous section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 65.46,
          "en": "Though, as a React developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.46,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "you should know about both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "because you will encounter both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 72.96000000000001,
          "en": "out there in the wild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.96000000000001,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now, in this section, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "I'll introduce you to this form actions feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 81,
          "en": "I'll explain how you can use it and what it's all about,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "and you will learn how you can use this React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "to extract values and manage form state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 91.44,
          "en": "You will learn how to set up and deal with synchronous",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.44,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "and asynchronous actions, and you will learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 98.65,
          "en": "how you can implement optimistic updating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.65,
          "end": 102.78,
          "en": "into your user interface with help of this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.78,
          "end": 104.913,
          "en": "and with help of React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 108.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.21000000000001,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "we'll use a brand new starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "which you'll find attached, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "And this starting project is very similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 120.87,
          "en": "to the project you saw in the previous section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.87,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "It's just a slightly simplified version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "if you want to call it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "because here I just have this signup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 132.033,
          "en": "component with that signup form you already know though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.96,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "But I got no login form because you already know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "how you can handle forms in general.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 141.69,
          "en": "But in this section you'll now learn about an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 143.943,
          "en": "because you'll learn about form actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.78,
          "end": 146.49,
          "en": "Now in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.49,
          "end": 149.43,
          "en": "if you're using the local version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.43,
          "end": 151.32,
          "en": "you of course should download it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.32,
          "end": 154.683,
          "en": "and then run npm install to install all dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 159.423,
          "en": "and then run npm run dev to start that development server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.53,
          "end": 164.25,
          "en": "And if you then visit local host 5173,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 167.34300000000002,
          "en": "you should see a page like this on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
